Bug: `dict.fromkeys(..., [])` gives every key the same list object, so all groups alias one list. Also, `map(key, items)` consumes a generator, so the second loop sees nothing. Fix: one pass, `setdefault` creates a fresh list per key.

```python
def group_by(items, key):
    """Return {key(item): [items]} with groups in first-seen key order and items in input order. items may be any iterable (including a generator, consumed once). Does not modify items."""
    groups = {}
    for item in items:
        groups.setdefault(key(item), []).append(item)
    return groups
```

